Because knowing and saying are different operations. The lecture’s central claim is not that they are identical, but that they can be connected more strongly. That gives us a useful final contrast: $\begin{aligned}
\text{I do not know} &\Longrightarrow \text{silence of ignorance},\\
\text{I know, but cannot transfer it} &\Longrightarrow \text{silence of weak connection}.\end{aligned}$ This lecture is about the second case.

